{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"id\":\"N114\",\"lines\":\"--n-n\"}\n{\"id\":\"N114.3\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"أَطَعْنَكُمْ\",\"target_ar\":\"نُشُوزَهُنَّ\",\"after\":\"The feared rise is pictured as a neck lengthening.\",\"reason\":\"سَطْع is length of the neck; نُشُوز is rising or protrusion. They share a vertical image, though broadly.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N114.5\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"أَطَعْنَكُمْ\",\"target_ar\":\"عَلِيًّا\",\"after\":\"A long neck and divine height share an upward line.\",\"reason\":\"سَطْع is physical neck length, while عَلِيًّا is exalted height. The link is a general vertical echo.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N115\",\"lines\":\"r-r\"}\n{\"id\":\"N115.1\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"أَطَعْنَكُمْ\",\"target_ar\":\"ٱلرِّجَالُ\",\"after\":\"The tent pillar stands beside the bodily leg. Together they make the men’s legs seem like supports holding a structure upright.\",\"reason\":\"ٱلسِّطَاع is a tent pillar, and ٱلرِّجَالُ is glossed here as the leg. Each is a vertical support, one built and one bodily.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N115.3\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"أَطَعْنَكُمْ\",\"target_ar\":\"عَلِيًّا\",\"after\":\"The tent pillar gives physical form to the coda’s height. The image lets divine highness appear as a support rising above the household scene.\",\"reason\":\"ٱلسِّطَاع is an upright tent column; عَلِيًّا is height or exaltation. Their shared upward form makes an image of a high support.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N116\",\"lines\":\"--n-\"}\n{\"id\":\"N116.3\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"أَطَعْنَكُمْ\",\"target_ar\":\"أَمْوَٰلِهِمْ\",\"after\":\"The spent assets can be pictured as branded livestock.\",\"reason\":\"ٱلسِّطَاع is a lengthwise mark on a camel’s neck; أَمْوَٰلِهِمْ is their wealth. The brand marks an animal as property, a narrow image of an asset.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N117\",\"lines\":\"nrn\"}\n{\"id\":\"N117.1\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"أَطَعْنَكُمْ\",\"target_ar\":\"نُشُوزَهُنَّ\",\"after\":\"A raised sound meets a bodily rise.\",\"reason\":\"ٱلسَّطْع is the high sound of a strike; نُشُوز is elevation or protrusion. Their shared upward quality is an acoustic and physical echo.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N117.2\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"sound\",\"focus_ar\":\"أَطَعْنَكُمْ\",\"target_ar\":\"وَٱضْرِبُوهُنَّ\",\"after\":\"The strike is heard as an event with a sharp report. Its sound makes the command audible in the very act it names.\",\"reason\":\"ٱلسَّطْع is the sound raised by a blow, and وَٱضْرِبُوهُنَّ names striking. The rare sense supplies the blow’s answering sound.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N117.3\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"أَطَعْنَكُمْ\",\"target_ar\":\"كَبِيرًا\",\"after\":\"The great is paired with a loud sound.\",\"reason\":\"ٱلسَّطْع is a strike’s high sound; كَبِيرًا is bigness. Loudness can suggest magnitude, but the link is broad.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N118\",\"lines\":\"---\"}\n{\"id\":\"N119\",\"lines\":\"r--\"}\n{\"id\":\"N119.1\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"أَطَعْنَكُمْ\",\"target_ar\":\"قَٰنِتَٰتٌ\",\"after\":\"Their compliance answers the quality of devotion. The verse lets obedience appear both as a settled disposition and as an act toward the addressed group.\",\"reason\":\"طَاعَتُهُنَّ is compliance or mutual agreement; قَٰنِتَٰتٌ is devotional obedience. The two senses meet in willing submission.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N120\",\"lines\":\"n-n\"}\n{\"id\":\"N120.1\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"part\",\"focus_ar\":\"أَطَعْنَكُمْ\",\"target_ar\":\"قَٰنِتَٰتٌ\",\"after\":\"Capacity is a condition for obedience.\",\"reason\":\"ٱلِاسْتِطَاعَة is ability to act; قَٰنِتَٰتٌ is devotional obedience. Ability enables obedience, though the relation is general.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N120.3\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"part\",\"focus_ar\":\"أَطَعْنَكُمْ\",\"target_ar\":\"كَانَ\",\"after\":\"What can be done can then come to pass.\",\"reason\":\"ٱلِاسْتِطَاعَة is capacity, while كَانَ signals occurrence or being. Capacity can be a stage before realization.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N121\",\"lines\":\"--n\"}\n{\"id\":\"N121.3\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"opposite\",\"focus_ar\":\"أَطَعْنَكُمْ\",\"target_ar\":\"ٱلْمَضَاجِعِ\",\"after\":\"Striving to become able contrasts with lying down.\",\"reason\":\"تَكَلُّفُ الِاسْتِطَاعَة is exerting oneself to manage a task; ٱلْمَضَاجِعِ evokes lying on one’s side. Effort and repose form a broad opposition.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N122\",\"lines\":\"r-r---\"}\n{\"id\":\"N122.1\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"أَطَعْنَكُمْ\",\"target_ar\":\"فَضَّلَ\",\"after\":\"Voluntary goodness meets the surplus or gift in فَضَّلَ. The pairing makes bounty sound like giving beyond what is owed.\",\"reason\":\"ٱلتَّطَوُّع is good done freely beyond an obligation; فَضَّلَ carries the sense of increase or gift. Both point to what exceeds a due.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N122.3\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"أَطَعْنَكُمْ\",\"target_ar\":\"أَنفَقُوا۟\",\"after\":\"The spending can be heard as a freely offered gift. This brings the voluntary good of the rare sense into the verse’s stated expenditure.\",\"reason\":\"ٱلتَّطَوُّع is voluntary giving beyond what is required; أَنفَقُوا۟ means they spent or caused wealth to go out. The voluntary gift is one kind of spending.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N123\",\"lines\":\"-nn-r-\"}\n{\"id\":\"N123.2\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"أَطَعْنَكُمْ\",\"target_ar\":\"قَٰنِتَٰتٌ\",\"after\":\"An inward easing can lead toward obedience.\",\"reason\":\"تَطْوِيعُ النَّفْس is the self making an act easy or answering it; قَٰنِتَٰتٌ names devotional obedience. The connection is real but general.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N123.3\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"part\",\"focus_ar\":\"أَطَعْنَكُمْ\",\"target_ar\":\"حَٰفِظَٰتٌ\",\"after\":\"The self’s readiness can help make guarding possible.\",\"reason\":\"تَطْوِيعُ النَّفْس is inward encouragement or ease; حَٰفِظَٰتٌ are ongoing guardians. Readiness may support the act of guarding, a broad link.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N123.5\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"part\",\"focus_ar\":\"أَطَعْنَكُمْ\",\"target_ar\":\"وَٱضْرِبُوهُنَّ\",\"after\":\"The command to strike meets the possibility that the self makes an act easy. The pairing puts inward encouragement beside the outward imperative, making the deed’s inner assent audible.\",\"reason\":\"طَوَّعَتْ لَهُ نَفْسُهُ means that one’s self made an act easy or encouraged it; وَٱضْرِبُوهُنَّ commands a blow. Inner facilitation can be a stage in carrying out that act.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N124\",\"lines\":\"---\"}\n{\"id\":\"N125\",\"lines\":\"rn-r-\"}\n{\"id\":\"N125.1\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"تَبْغُوا۟\",\"target_ar\":\"فَٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتُ\",\"after\":\"Soundness and fitness meet in the صالحات. The pairing makes the good women those who are fittingly ordered toward what is right.\",\"reason\":\"مَا يَنْبَغِي is what is fitting or ought to be; فَٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتُ names soundness and rectitude. Both senses converge on fitness.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N125.2\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"تَبْغُوا۟\",\"target_ar\":\"قَٰنِتَٰتٌ\",\"after\":\"Devotion can be heard as what is fitting.\",\"reason\":\"مَا يَنْبَغِي means what ought to be; قَٰنِتَٰتٌ are devoted in obedience. This is a broad link between fitting conduct and devotion.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N125.4\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"تَبْغُوا۟\",\"target_ar\":\"أَطَعْنَكُمْ\",\"after\":\"When they comply, no further way against them is fitting. The rare sense of what ought to be gives the halt a measure of propriety.\",\"reason\":\"مَا يَنْبَغِي is what is suitable or ought to be; أَطَعْنَكُمْ is their compliance. The condition and the sense of propriety complete each other in the command not to pursue a way against them.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N126\",\"lines\":\"-nrrrr\"}\n{\"id\":\"N126.2\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"تَبْغُوا۟\",\"target_ar\":\"فَضَّلَ\",\"after\":\"Both senses touch excess, with different force.\",\"reason\":\"بَغْي is crossing a limit; فَضْل carries increase or surplus. The overlap is excess, but one is wrongful overreach and the other a granted distinction.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N126.3\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"opposite\",\"focus_ar\":\"تَبْغُوا۟\",\"target_ar\":\"فَٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتُ\",\"after\":\"The verse places soundness beside the danger of corruption and excess. That opposition makes the sound women a measure against transgression.\",\"reason\":\"بَغْي is corruption or exceeding a limit, while فَٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتُ names soundness and rectitude. These senses stand as opposites.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N126.4\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"part\",\"focus_ar\":\"تَبْغُوا۟\",\"target_ar\":\"وَٱضْرِبُوهُنَّ\",\"after\":\"The prohibition on overstepping can be heard beside the preceding strike. It makes the blow answerable to a boundary, so it cannot become transgression.\",\"reason\":\"بَغْي is unjust aggression and passing a limit; وَٱضْرِبُوهُنَّ is a striking act. A blow can become a means of aggression when it crosses the limit.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N126.5\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"opposite\",\"focus_ar\":\"تَبْغُوا۟\",\"target_ar\":\"عَلِيًّا\",\"after\":\"Human overreach is set beside divine highness. The contrast makes the prohibition a check on claiming the elevation that belongs to God.\",\"reason\":\"بَغْي includes arrogant overstepping; عَلِيًّا names exalted height. Wrongful self-elevation stands against divine exaltation.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N126.6\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"opposite\",\"focus_ar\":\"تَبْغُوا۟\",\"target_ar\":\"كَبِيرًا\",\"after\":\"The ban on arrogant excess closes with God’s greatness. Human self-aggrandizement is diminished beside the greatness named at the end.\",\"reason\":\"بَغْي can mean transgression through arrogance; كَبِيرًا names greatness. The ayah contrasts human overreach with divine magnitude.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N127\",\"lines\":\"-rnr-\"}\n{\"id\":\"N127.2\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"opposite\",\"focus_ar\":\"تَبْغُوا۟\",\"target_ar\":\"فَٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتُ\",\"after\":\"A sound state stands opposite a wound that swells into corruption. The image sharpens the difference between what is صالح and what has begun to rot.\",\"reason\":\"بَغَى الجُرْح is a wound swelling or closing with corruption inside; فَٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتُ is soundness opposed to فساد. The senses directly oppose one another.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N127.3\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"تَبْغُوا۟\",\"target_ar\":\"وَٱهْجُرُوهُنَّ\",\"after\":\"Separation meets a wound that closes over corruption.\",\"reason\":\"بَغَى الجُرْح describes a wound that seals while retaining corruption; وَٱهْجُرُوهُنَّ is separation. The pair suggests an estrangement that closes outwardly while festering within.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N127.4\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"تَبْغُوا۟\",\"target_ar\":\"وَٱضْرِبُوهُنَّ\",\"after\":\"The strike stands beside the wound that swells and rots. Together they make a picture of injury whose harm can grow beyond the moment of impact.\",\"reason\":\"بَغَى الجُرْح is an inflamed or corrupted wound; وَٱضْرِبُوهُنَّ names striking. A blow can make the wound in the rare sense.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N128\",\"lines\":\"n--\"}\n{\"id\":\"N128.1\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"تَبْغُوا۟\",\"target_ar\":\"لِّلْغَيْبِ\",\"after\":\"Sexual misconduct can be hidden from sight.\",\"reason\":\"ٱلْبَغَاء is illicit sexual conduct; ٱلْغَيْبِ is what is absent or unseen. A concealed affair fits the hidden domain, though secrecy is not part of the rare gloss itself.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N129\",\"lines\":\"rnrn\"}\n{\"id\":\"N129.1\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"تَبْغُوا۟\",\"target_ar\":\"فَضَّلَ\",\"after\":\"The excess of a heavy rain meets the surplus in فَضْل. The ayah’s language can make divine increase feel like a force that pours beyond need.\",\"reason\":\"بَغْيُ المَطَر is rain in its intensity and abundance, even beyond need; فَضْل is increase or surplus. Both describe excess, here as rainfall and bounty.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N129.2\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"تَبْغُوا۟\",\"target_ar\":\"وَٱضْرِبُوهُنَّ\",\"after\":\"A heavy downpour can be pictured as striking its surface.\",\"reason\":\"بَغْيُ المَطَر is abundant, forceful rain; وَٱضْرِبُوهُنَّ names a blow. The image of rain striking ground offers a broad echo of impact.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N129.3\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"تَبْغُوا۟\",\"target_ar\":\"سَبِيلًا\",\"after\":\"The rain makes a descending course between cloud and earth. Alongside سَبِيلًا, the image turns a way into a path of water through the air.\",\"reason\":\"بَغْيُ السَّمَاءِ is heavy rain, described as falling between cloud and earth; سَبِيلًا is a path or way. The falling rain gives that way a concrete course.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N129.4\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"تَبْغُوا۟\",\"target_ar\":\"كَبِيرًا\",\"after\":\"The great rain meets the word for great.\",\"reason\":\"بَغْيُ المَطَر is a great abundance of rain; كَبِيرًا is bigness. The overlap is clear but broad.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N130\",\"lines\":\"r--\"}\n{\"id\":\"N130.1\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"part\",\"focus_ar\":\"تَبْغُوا۟\",\"target_ar\":\"ٱلرِّجَالُ\",\"after\":\"The prancing horse is carried forward by its legs. This makes the leg itself part of the lively gait named by the rare sense.\",\"reason\":\"بَغْيُ الفَرَس is proud, playful running; ٱلرِّجَالُ is glossed here as the leg. The leg is an instrument of the horse’s run.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N131\",\"lines\":\"nrnn--\"}\n{\"id\":\"N131.1\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"part\",\"focus_ar\":\"تَبْغُوا۟\",\"target_ar\":\"قَوَّٰمُونَ\",\"after\":\"A vanguard is a forward part of a larger company.\",\"reason\":\"ٱلْبَغَايَا are troops that go ahead of an army; قَوَّٰمُونَ is glossed here as a group of people and men. The advance troops can be pictured within such a group.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N131.2\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"part\",\"focus_ar\":\"تَبْغُوا۟\",\"target_ar\":\"حَٰفِظَٰتٌ\",\"after\":\"A vanguard can watch ahead for the people behind it. This turns the image of guarding into a small unit moving out in front.\",\"reason\":\"ٱلْبَغَايَا are scouts or advance troops; حَٰفِظَٰتٌ are guardians. The vanguard is an instrument of protection.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N131.3\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"part\",\"focus_ar\":\"تَبْغُوا۟\",\"target_ar\":\"حَفِظَ\",\"after\":\"Advance troops can serve the work of preservation.\",\"reason\":\"ٱلْبَغَايَا are troops sent ahead; حَفِظَ means to guard or preserve. The troop can act as a means of protection, though the divine agent makes the link broad.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N131.4\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"تَبْغُوا۟\",\"target_ar\":\"تَخَافُونَ\",\"after\":\"Fear can call for a vanguard to go ahead.\",\"reason\":\"ٱلْبَغَايَا are advance troops; تَخَافُونَ is apprehension of possible harm. The two fit a danger-and-scouting scene.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N132\",\"lines\":\"-n-\"}\n{\"id\":\"N132.2\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"سَبِيلًا\",\"target_ar\":\"حَٰفِظَٰتٌ\",\"after\":\"A traveller on the road may be watched over.\",\"reason\":\"ٱلسَّابِلَة are people who travel the roads; حَٰفِظَٰتٌ are guardians. Travellers and protectors complement each other, though the connection is general.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N133\",\"lines\":\"rrr\"}\n{\"id\":\"N133.1\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"سَبِيلًا\",\"target_ar\":\"ٱلرِّجَالُ\",\"after\":\"A garment released from above falls along the leg. The men’s bodily image gives the downward drape a human line.\",\"reason\":\"إِسْبَال is letting a garment or cloth fall downward; ٱلرِّجَالُ is glossed here as the leg. The hanging cloth can be seen descending alongside the leg.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N133.2\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"سَبِيلًا\",\"target_ar\":\"ٱلْمَضَاجِعِ\",\"after\":\"The drape falls from above onto the place where bodies lie. Together the senses make an image of a curtain lowered over a bed.\",\"reason\":\"إِسْبَال is sending something down from above; ٱلْمَضَاجِعِ are lying-down places. The bed supplies the lower place where the hanging thing comes to rest.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N133.3\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"opposite\",\"focus_ar\":\"سَبِيلًا\",\"target_ar\":\"عَلِيًّا\",\"after\":\"The cloth or rain descends from above while the coda names exalted height. Their opposed directions make the high-and-low axis audible across the verse.\",\"reason\":\"إِسْبَال is lowering or letting something fall; عَلِيًّا is height and exaltation. Downward release opposes upward elevation.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N134\",\"lines\":\"rr-\"}\n{\"id\":\"N134.1\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"سَبِيلًا\",\"target_ar\":\"ٱلْمَضَاجِعِ\",\"after\":\"Rain falls from cloud toward earth, where bodies lie. The two senses make the bed a receiving place beneath a descending sky.\",\"reason\":\"ٱلسَّبْل is rain falling between cloud and earth; ٱلْمَضَاجِعِ are places of lying down. The bed and the rain’s downward course meet in one image.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N134.2\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"سَبِيلًا\",\"target_ar\":\"وَٱضْرِبُوهُنَّ\",\"after\":\"The rain is pictured striking the earth, while the command names a blow. This makes the force of falling water answer the force of impact in the verse.\",\"reason\":\"ٱلسَّبْل is abundant rain; وَٱضْرِبُوهُنَّ is striking. Rainfall’s impact on the earth makes a shared picture of force landing on a surface.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N135\",\"lines\":\"--n\"}\n{\"id\":\"N135.3\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"سَبِيلًا\",\"target_ar\":\"عَلِيًّا\",\"after\":\"A hanging strand descends from the upper face.\",\"reason\":\"ٱلسَّبَل is hair hanging from the upper lip or beard; عَلِيًّا is height. The high location and downward hair form a slight top-to-bottom image.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N136\",\"lines\":\"r-n\"}\n{\"id\":\"N136.1\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"part\",\"focus_ar\":\"سَبِيلًا\",\"target_ar\":\"أَنفَقُوا۟\",\"after\":\"The vessel’s rim is where its contents can pour out. This makes the rare edge image a point of departure for the wealth that is spent.\",\"reason\":\"ٱلسَّبَلَة is the vessel’s lip or rim; أَنفَقُوا۟ means spending or causing wealth to go out. The rim is the outlet for what flows from a full vessel.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N136.3\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"سَبِيلًا\",\"target_ar\":\"عَلِيًّا\",\"after\":\"The raised rim meets the coda’s height.\",\"reason\":\"ٱلسَّبَلَة can be the upper edge of a vessel; عَلِيًّا is exalted or high. Both carry a high-position image, though the link is general.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N137\",\"lines\":\"-r-\"}\n{\"id\":\"N137.2\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"سَبِيلًا\",\"target_ar\":\"أَمْوَٰلِهِمْ\",\"after\":\"The grain head is a harvest that can become wealth. The pairing makes the assets spent in the verse carry an image of ripened fields.\",\"reason\":\"إِسْبَالُ الزَّرْع is the crop sending out its grain head; أَمْوَٰلِهِمْ is their wealth and assets. A harvested crop is one concrete source of wealth.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N138\",\"lines\":\"-r-\"}\n{\"id\":\"N138.2\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"سَبِيلًا\",\"target_ar\":\"لِّلْغَيْبِ\",\"after\":\"The diseased veil in the eye clouds what can be seen. Beside the hidden domain, it makes absence feel like a screen over vision.\",\"reason\":\"ٱلسَّبَل is a web-like veil in the eye; ٱلْغَيْبِ is what is hidden from sight or knowledge. The eye disease physically veils what would otherwise be seen.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N139\",\"lines\":\"--rr\"}\n{\"id\":\"N139.3\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"ٱللَّهَ\",\"target_ar\":\"عَلِيًّا\",\"after\":\"Allah’s name can be heard as a call, and عَلِيًّا names height. Together they make the coda sound like an address to the Most High.\",\"reason\":\"ٱللَّه is given as a name used in invocation or calling; عَلِيًّا means exalted or high. The name and height predicate complete each other as an address and attribute.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N139.4\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"ٱللَّهَ\",\"target_ar\":\"كَبِيرًا\",\"after\":\"The name of Allah meets the predicate of greatness. The closing words can be heard as invoking the One who is great.\",\"reason\":\"ٱللَّه is a divine name used in oath or invocation; كَبِيرًا names greatness. The divine name and quality belong together.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N140\",\"lines\":\"nn-\"}\n{\"id\":\"N140.1\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"كَانَ\",\"target_ar\":\"قَوَّٰمُونَ\",\"after\":\"A social place complements a group’s standing.\",\"reason\":\"ٱلْمَكَانَة is position or status; قَوَّٰمُونَ is glossed here as a group of people and men. A group has a social place, though the relation is broad.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N140.2\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"كَانَ\",\"target_ar\":\"فَضَّلَ\",\"after\":\"Rank can be heard as a kind of surplus.\",\"reason\":\"ٱلْمَكَانَة is status or rank; فَضَّلَ carries increase or surplus. The senses meet loosely in having more standing.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N141\",\"lines\":\"-rrrn\"}\n{\"id\":\"N141.2\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"كَانَ\",\"target_ar\":\"حَٰفِظَٰتٌ\",\"after\":\"The guardians preserve what they have undertaken to protect. The pairing gives their keeping the weight of an accepted responsibility.\",\"reason\":\"كَفَالَة is guaranteeing or taking responsibility for someone; حَٰفِظَٰتٌ are guardians and preservers. Both describe sustained care.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N141.3\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"كَانَ\",\"target_ar\":\"حَفِظَ\",\"after\":\"Divine preservation can be heard as an undertaking to care for what is guarded. This links the act of keeping with the assumption of responsibility.\",\"reason\":\"كَفَالَة is sponsorship or taking someone under one’s care; حَفِظَ means God guarded or preserved. The senses meet in responsible protection.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N141.4\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"opposite\",\"focus_ar\":\"كَانَ\",\"target_ar\":\"وَٱضْرِبُوهُنَّ\",\"after\":\"The undertaking of responsibility stands beside the command to strike. Hearing both exposes a tension between taking someone into one’s care and using force against them.\",\"reason\":\"كَفَلَ بِفُلَانٍ means to assume responsibility for someone; وَٱضْرِبُوهُنَّ directs a blow at them. Care and inflicted force pull in opposite directions.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N141.5\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"كَانَ\",\"target_ar\":\"عَلِيًّا\",\"after\":\"The human undertaking sits beneath the divine height.\",\"reason\":\"كَفَالَة is taking responsibility for another; عَلِيًّا names exalted height. A human caretaker and the higher divine guarantor complement each other.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N142\",\"lines\":\"r-r\"}\n{\"id\":\"N142.1\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"كَانَ\",\"target_ar\":\"قَٰنِتَٰتٌ\",\"after\":\"The rare sense of submission answers the devoted obedience named in قَٰنِتَٰتٌ. The quality and the root image say one yielding act in different words.\",\"reason\":\"ٱلِاسْتِكَانَة is submission or humble yielding; قَٰنِتَٰتٌ names obedient devotion. Both express submission.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N142.3\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"كَانَ\",\"target_ar\":\"أَطَعْنَكُمْ\",\"after\":\"Their compliance can be heard as yielding. The two senses give the conditional halt an echo of submission.\",\"reason\":\"ٱلِاسْتِكَانَة is humble submission; أَطَعْنَكُمْ means they complied or obeyed. The senses meet in yielding to another.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N143\",\"lines\":\"--r\"}\n{\"id\":\"N143.3\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"كَانَ\",\"target_ar\":\"كَبِيرًا\",\"after\":\"The old person who speaks from youth meets the language of greatness. The close can make كبير carry the fullness of age as well as size.\",\"reason\":\"كُنْتِيّ is an old man recalling what he was in youth; كَبِيرًا names bigness and can evoke advanced age. The shared age image brings the elder and the great together.\"}"}}
